CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* auto deduces std::initializer_list: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* elements decay: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* namespace scope: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* in a template: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [dcl.type.auto.deduct]/4: `auto il = {1, 2, 3};' deduces
std::initializer_list<int>.  The list was deduced as an array `int[3]', so
il.size() was rejected and sizeof(il) was 12.
